- description: The Docstring Coverage Band metric evaluates the presence and quality of docstrings within functions and classes in a codebase. It measures the extent to which these elements are documented, identifying areas where documentation is missing or incomplete. This metric encompasses all public and private methods and classes, ensuring a comprehensive assessment of the code's documentation practices. It serves as an indicator of code maintainability and usability, as well-documented code is easier for developers to understand and use. By flagging insufficient documentation, this metric encourages adherence to best practices in software development and promotes clearer communication within teams.

