- description: This metric evaluates the existence and quality of test files within a code repository, providing insights into the robustness of the testing practices employed. It measures whether unit tests, integration tests, and end-to-end tests are present, as well as the extent to which the codebase is covered by these tests. The metric also assesses the quality of the tests, including factors such as the clarity of test cases and the effectiveness of assertions. By analyzing both the presence of tests and their coverage, this metric helps identify potential gaps in testing that could lead to undetected bugs or vulnerabilities. Overall, it serves as an indicator of the reliability and maintainability of the software being developed.

