Metric:
- id: repo.deployment_readiness
- name: Deployment Readiness
- description: Deployment Readiness measures the effectiveness and reliability of deployment scripts and automation processes within a code repository. It evaluates the completeness and correctness of the scripts that facilitate the deployment of applications, ensuring that they can be executed without errors. This metric also assesses the mechanisms in place for rolling back deployments in case of failures, which is critical for maintaining system stability. The scope includes both the automation tools used and the configuration settings that govern deployment behavior. Typical signals include the presence of automated tests, version control practices, and documentation related to deployment procedures.

