- description: The Experiments Management metric evaluates the organization and standardization of machine learning experiments within a code repository. It inspects the presence and structure of experiment directories and configuration files, which are essential for tracking and reproducing experiments. This metric focuses on the clarity and consistency of naming conventions, the use of version control for experiment configurations, and the documentation of experimental setups. By assessing these aspects, the metric provides insights into the reproducibility of results and the ease with which other team members can understand and replicate experiments. A well-managed experiments framework is crucial for collaborative ML projects, ensuring that findings can be reliably reproduced and built upon.

