- id: feature_engineering
- name: Feature Engineering Hygiene
- description: Feature Engineering Hygiene measures the quality and consistency of the feature engineering processes used in machine learning workflows. It focuses on ensuring that the features created during the training phase are reproducible and match those used during model serving or inference. This metric evaluates the code for adherence to best practices that promote reproducibility, such as version control of feature definitions and consistent data preprocessing steps. Additionally, it assesses the parity between training and serving environments to prevent discrepancies that could lead to model performance degradation. By monitoring this metric, teams can identify potential issues that may arise from feature drift or misalignment, ultimately supporting the reliability and robustness of deployed models.

