- description: This metric evaluates the practices surrounding hyperparameter tuning in machine learning workflows, specifically focusing on frameworks such as Optuna and Ray Tune. It measures the effectiveness of the hyperparameter optimization setup, including the strategies employed for searching the hyperparameter space and the methodologies used to assess model performance. Additionally, the metric assesses the reproducibility of the tuning process, ensuring that the same hyperparameter configurations can yield consistent results across different runs. It also examines the persistence of the best configurations, verifying that optimal hyperparameters are documented and can be reliably retrieved for future use. Overall, this metric provides insights into the robustness and reliability of hyperparameter optimization practices within machine learning projects.

