Metric:
- id: ml.data_validation
- name: Data Validation
- description: Data Validation measures the integrity and quality of data as it flows through machine learning pipelines. It focuses on three primary aspects: schema validation, which checks if the data conforms to the expected structure; range validation, which ensures that the data values fall within predefined acceptable limits; and drift validation, which identifies shifts in data distribution over time that may affect model performance. This metric highlights any missing quality gates that should be implemented to ensure data reliability. Additionally, it assesses the integration of continuous integration (CI) practices to automate data quality checks. Overall, Data Validation serves as a critical checkpoint to maintain high standards of data quality throughout the ML workflow.

